1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:05,922
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,636 --> 00:00:14,681
[Natalie] <i>You can't live</i>
<i>without your wife.</i>

3
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:15,932
[Raul] <i>Trust me.</i>

4
00:00:16,016 --> 00:00:19,394
<i>If you trust me then you need</i>
<i>to lie low for a while.</i>

5
00:00:19,477 --> 00:00:21,062
<i>Natalie, you're in danger.</i>

6
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:24,190
[Claire] <i>If Jaguar is an enemy,</i>
<i>why'd he let Emilia go?</i>

7
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:28,528
[Julio] <i>To send a message</i>
<i>that we are at his mercy.</i>

8
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:31,698
<i>I won't allow the collusion of Diego</i>

9
00:00:31,781 --> 00:00:35,160
<i>or some hotsie-patootsie woman</i>
<i>like Natalie</i>

10
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:37,203
<i>to ruin the name Ardiente.</i>

11
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:38,997
[Ivy] <i>Is Diego working with Jaguar?</i>

12
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:41,124
<i>If they continue to work together,</i>

13
00:00:41,207 --> 00:00:43,251
<i>I might lose the election.</i>

14
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,504
[Raul] <i>It's just gonna be the two of us.</i>

15
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:48,548
[Julio] <i>Should you get the chance,</i>

16
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:50,759
<i>I want you to kill that SOB,</i>

17
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:52,719
<i>so I won't have any more problems.</i>

18
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,054
[Emilia] <i>But with one condition.</i>

19
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:57,390
<i>You will allow me</i>
<i>to replace you in Congress.</i>

20
00:00:57,474 --> 00:01:00,560
[Camia] <i>Does that mean Diego can go free?</i>

21
00:01:00,643 --> 00:01:02,979
<i>Only if he agrees to my offer,</i>

22
00:01:03,063 --> 00:01:06,816
<i>to tap Jaguar as his financier</i>
<i>in the election.</i>

23
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:10,987
<i>I'd rather rot in prison</i>
<i>than become Jaguar's lapdog.</i>

24
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:13,323
<i>I'll find a way to free Diego.</i>

25
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:18,036
<i>But first, I need to find out</i>
<i>the identity of Jaguar.</i>

26
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:20,497
[Julio] <i>You will all grace</i>
<i>a public appearance.</i>

27
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:24,459
<i>I don't want another scandal tomorrow,</i>
<i>so behave. Especially you, Emilia.</i>

28
00:01:24,542 --> 00:01:27,837
[Emilia] <i>Let's look for a place</i>
<i>without trashes lying around.</i>

29
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:29,798
-<i>You're the trash here!</i>
<i>-Shut up!</i>

30
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:32,383
[Camia] <i>Your family's downfall</i>
<i>is within reach.</i>

31
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:34,260
<i>We will win this election!</i>

32
00:01:34,344 --> 00:01:35,887
[Diego] <i>I need to get out of here.</i>

33
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:38,139
<i>I'm dragging Aunt Camia in this mess.</i>

34
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:40,934
[Arnaldo] <i>I promise you,</i>
<i>I will save our position.</i>

35
00:01:41,017 --> 00:01:42,560
<i>I'll take care of our name.</i>

36
00:01:42,644 --> 00:01:45,522
<i>The Ardientes will continue</i>
<i>to rule this town.</i>

37
00:01:49,692 --> 00:01:51,152
-Oh.
-Wow!

38
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:54,405
He's got taste, Auntie.

39
00:01:54,823 --> 00:01:56,282
[Claire] And the other one?

40
00:02:00,912 --> 00:02:02,622
-Ah!
-[chuckles]

41
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:05,792
I don't know, Emilia.

42
00:02:06,417 --> 00:02:08,878
But that Jaguar seems shady.

43
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:12,215
He's like a guard dog stalking you.

44
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:14,175
And he knows what you want.

45
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:16,302
But you know, Auntie,

46
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:19,222
I like a man who knows
how to please his woman.

47
00:02:19,931 --> 00:02:20,974
Goodness.

48
00:02:22,142 --> 00:02:24,602
You're falling for that
masked creature, Emilia.

49
00:02:25,311 --> 00:02:28,439
[laughing] Of course not, Auntie.

50
00:02:28,523 --> 00:02:30,275
It's the other way around.

51
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:32,110
He is falling for me.

52
00:02:34,112 --> 00:02:36,156
[phone chiming]

53
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:39,409
-Look who's calling.
-[chuckling]

54
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:42,120
I told you, Auntie. Let me take it.

55
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:45,165
Jaguar, Jaguar.

56
00:02:46,499 --> 00:02:48,209
You just really know how to please me.

57
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:49,836
I love all the gifts.

58
00:02:50,378 --> 00:02:52,463
-I love it.
-It's only for…

59
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:54,173
[voice changer] <i>woman like you.</i>

60
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:57,093
Oh, come on.

61
00:02:57,552 --> 00:03:00,763
I know you want something
in exchange, right?

62
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:02,891
That's what I like about you, Emilia.

63
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:04,642
I can't get enough of you.

64
00:03:05,685 --> 00:03:06,978
<i>You're very smart.</i>

65
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:08,313
What do you want from me?

66
00:03:09,814 --> 00:03:12,150
I want to get a whiff of your sweet scent.

67
00:03:12,775 --> 00:03:13,735
[smirks]

68
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:18,364
You're making me blush. Can you stop it?

69
00:03:18,948 --> 00:03:19,866
Can you please tell me,

70
00:03:19,949 --> 00:03:21,868
what exactly do you want from me?

71
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:25,997
Have you thought about my proposition?

72
00:03:27,081 --> 00:03:28,666
I don't know yet.

73
00:03:29,959 --> 00:03:31,294
Emilia, I'm impatient.

74
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:33,796
You never know,

75
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:36,591
<i>someone else might catch my attention.</i>

76
00:03:36,674 --> 00:03:37,967
<i>It's your call.</i>

77
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:40,136
Okay fine, Jaguar.

78
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:44,515
After our kick-off campaign

79
00:03:44,599 --> 00:03:46,768
and the engagement party of my son,

80
00:03:46,851 --> 00:03:48,228
you'll know my decision.

81
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:51,856
And I'm sure, you won't be disappointed.

82
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:54,984
Okay, my love. I'll wait for it.

83
00:03:55,318 --> 00:03:56,778
Bye, Jaguar.

84
00:04:05,954 --> 00:04:08,164
How's the venue? Is everything set?

85
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:09,624
[woman] Not yet, sir.

86
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:11,209
We still don't have a sound system.

87
00:04:11,292 --> 00:04:12,377
What do you mean by that?

88
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,921
Isn't that the first thing you should fix?

89
00:04:15,672 --> 00:04:17,423
How will the people hear me
when I make a speech?

90
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:19,008
-I'm sorry.
-There you go again,

91
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:21,219
showing your incompetence. Get on it!

92
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:23,513
-[Ivy] Hon!
-[Arnaldo] Get out of my sight!

93
00:04:23,596 --> 00:04:24,764
[Ivy] Hon.

94
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:30,436
What's wrong?
You're losing your temper again.

95
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:33,690
-Hon, relax.
-[smooches]

96
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:36,109
There you go. Relax, okay?

97
00:04:36,192 --> 00:04:37,443
I'll try.

98
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:38,569
Hon,

99
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:41,364
everything will turn out fine tomorrow.

100
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:42,532
I promise.

101
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:45,034
-I promise you that.
-Okay.

102
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:48,746
Well, I need to meet with my designer

103
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:53,751
to try my outfit for tomorrow
because I want to look beautiful

104
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:56,045
for our engagement party tomorrow.

105
00:04:56,462 --> 00:04:58,840
-Okay, you go do that.
-Okay.

106
00:04:59,841 --> 00:05:00,883
Update me, okay?

107
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:03,761
-Bye, honey.
-Bye.

108
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:08,975
-Thank you, ma'am.
-All right.

109
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:18,276
-Judge Otico?
-Yes?

110
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:22,113
Who are you? Please, don't hurt me!

111
00:05:22,196 --> 00:05:24,866
Please, don't hurt me!

112
00:05:24,949 --> 00:05:27,327
Where are you taking me?
Please, don't hurt me!

113
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:29,037
Please, don't hurt me.

114
00:05:29,954 --> 00:05:31,456
Where are you taking me?

115
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:35,877
Judge Otico?

116
00:05:37,086 --> 00:05:39,213
Yes? Who are you?

117
00:05:39,964 --> 00:05:43,342
Let's just say that I am the nightmare

118
00:05:43,426 --> 00:05:45,219
of your boss, Jaguar.

119
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:50,892
Tell him to release Diego Torillo.

120
00:05:50,975 --> 00:05:52,685
I don't need to.

121
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:54,937
Torillo already met with Jaguar.

122
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:57,982
And they've probably come up
with an agreement.

123
00:06:00,443 --> 00:06:02,737
Please, let me go. Please.

124
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:04,072
Don't hurt me.

125
00:06:07,408 --> 00:06:08,451
Let her out.

126
00:06:11,788 --> 00:06:14,248
[Erlinda] Please, don't hurt me. Please.

127
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:15,708
Let's go!

128
00:06:15,958 --> 00:06:18,294
Where are you taking me?
Please, don't hurt me.

129
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:23,508
Please, don't hurt me. Please.

130
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:25,343
Let's go to the precinct.

131
00:06:41,901 --> 00:06:45,363
Jaguar says he doesn't want
to waste his time.

132
00:06:45,738 --> 00:06:49,242
He's hoping you're here
to accept his offer.

133
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:54,288
I accept your offer

134
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:56,290
but on one condition.

135
00:06:57,041 --> 00:06:58,084
If I win,

136
00:06:59,001 --> 00:07:00,962
you will shut down
all your illegal businesses

137
00:07:01,045 --> 00:07:02,046
in Ardiente.

138
00:07:02,713 --> 00:07:05,550
I will give you a chance
to put up new businesses.

139
00:07:06,717 --> 00:07:09,512
Legal businesses
that could help the public.

140
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,604
Diego, you have no right
to set conditions.

141
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:22,191
You are the one
who needs to follow his terms.

142
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:24,026
If that's the case,

143
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:29,407
tell your boss my sorry
for wasting his time.

144
00:07:32,618 --> 00:07:33,703
You know,

145
00:07:34,829 --> 00:07:37,582
the reason I am running
for governor here in Ardiente

146
00:07:37,665 --> 00:07:39,625
is because I want to change this town,

147
00:07:40,376 --> 00:07:41,919
not become a puppet

148
00:07:42,420 --> 00:07:45,339
of a man who's more ruthless
than the Ardientes.

149
00:07:45,423 --> 00:07:49,010
I don't know why you're so bent
on getting back at that family.

150
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:52,763
But I hope you're not doing
this simply for yourself,

151
00:07:53,973 --> 00:07:56,309
but for the people
you care about the most.

152
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:57,852
As for me,

153
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:03,524
I'm doing this to bring justice
for my murdered mother,

154
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:06,152
for what they did
to my best friend's family,

155
00:08:06,235 --> 00:08:08,988
and for neglecting the people of Ardiente!

156
00:08:09,071 --> 00:08:12,575
And most of all, to free my dad
from their leash

157
00:08:14,076 --> 00:08:16,871
and to be with the only family
that I have.

158
00:08:16,954 --> 00:08:19,832
[dramatic music playing]

159
00:08:35,389 --> 00:08:37,767
I want you to hang this
where everyone can see it.

160
00:08:37,850 --> 00:08:40,728
Like near the stage. Take note of that.

161
00:08:40,811 --> 00:08:41,812
Get on it.

162
00:08:47,818 --> 00:08:49,570
Lara, did you check on Ivy?

163
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:53,866
[Lara] Uh… Sir, Miss Aguas
didn't go to the atelier.

164
00:08:53,950 --> 00:08:56,369
They'll just deliver the dress
to her house.

165
00:09:01,165 --> 00:09:02,208
[Ivy] Diego.

166
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:04,502
Ivy.

167
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:06,629
What are you doing here?

168
00:09:11,384 --> 00:09:13,219
How's your meeting with Jaguar?

169
00:09:15,054 --> 00:09:16,889
-How did you know?
-It's a long story.

170
00:09:16,973 --> 00:09:20,017
I want to know
if you're getting out of here.

171
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:24,522
Ivy, we didn't come to an agreement.

172
00:09:27,066 --> 00:09:29,402
If that's the case,
I'll meet him personally.

173
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:31,946
Ivy, it's too…

174
00:09:36,784 --> 00:09:38,869
[Arnaldo] Who will you meet with, Ivy?

175
00:09:48,212 --> 00:09:53,301
Hon, I knew it. I knew you'd come here.

176
00:10:04,353 --> 00:10:05,354
Be safe.

177
00:10:18,492 --> 00:10:20,036
You haven't answered my question.

178
00:10:20,119 --> 00:10:21,078
Who will you talk to?

179
00:10:23,914 --> 00:10:24,874
Answer me!

180
00:10:26,709 --> 00:10:27,835
It's Camia Cruz.

181
00:10:28,711 --> 00:10:30,129
I wanted to talk to her

182
00:10:31,422 --> 00:10:35,009
to convince their party
to back out of the elections.

183
00:10:35,843 --> 00:10:40,640
-And why would you do that?
-Hon, let's face the reality.

184
00:10:41,182 --> 00:10:43,809
You conducted a survey, right? And what?

185
00:10:44,226 --> 00:10:48,606
Diego got 82 percent
while you got 18 percent.

186
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:50,524
Hon, you're going to lose!

187
00:10:50,941 --> 00:10:52,526
And I don't want you to get hurt!

188
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:54,779
You don't fight my battles, okay?!

189
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:56,405
You don't!

190
00:10:56,489 --> 00:10:58,699
Hon, I'm your future wife!

191
00:11:00,159 --> 00:11:01,911
Didn't you say we were a team?

192
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:04,580
So I'm just doing what's right!

193
00:11:06,123 --> 00:11:07,917
I just spoke to them.

194
00:11:09,043 --> 00:11:11,754
Hon, I want you to win.

195
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:17,635
[sighs] Okay.

196
00:11:18,719 --> 00:11:19,762
Okay.

197
00:11:20,221 --> 00:11:21,722
I'm sorry.

198
00:11:22,431 --> 00:11:24,058
I'm sorry for hurting you.

199
00:11:25,476 --> 00:11:27,728
All right, I admit that I was wrong.

200
00:11:28,437 --> 00:11:30,439
I was wrong for not telling you

201
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:31,857
that I was going to see Diego

202
00:11:31,941 --> 00:11:34,652
and that I wanted to talk to Camia.

203
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:40,950
Because, hon, I don't want you
to see me begging.

204
00:11:42,159 --> 00:11:47,957
Because I can lower
my ego and pride for you.

205
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:50,418
Because I really want you to win, hon.

206
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:56,298
Hon, trust me, it's the only reason.

207
00:11:57,842 --> 00:12:01,345
Hon, I love you so much.
That's why I'm marrying you.

208
00:12:03,097 --> 00:12:04,140
Hon.

209
00:12:05,057 --> 00:12:06,684
You don't believe me.

210
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:09,687
Hon.

211
00:12:13,357 --> 00:12:15,276
You don't believe me.

212
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:19,989
I'm getting scared.
You might get mad again.

213
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:26,287
Hon, maybe you'll get revenge
by calling off the wedding.

214
00:12:26,370 --> 00:12:28,289
Hon, please don't.

215
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:32,376
Arnaldo, please don't. Please.

216
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:34,211
Don't even think of canceling the wedding.

217
00:12:34,295 --> 00:12:35,880
Let's get married, hon.

218
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,548
I'm sorry. I won't do it again.

219
00:12:37,631 --> 00:12:40,468
I'll never visit Diego again. Never.

220
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:42,303
I'll never go near him.

221
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:44,597
Hon, please don't…

222
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:47,975
Arnaldo, please. Please.

223
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:50,644
I'm going crazy. Answer me, please!

224
00:12:50,728 --> 00:12:53,189
Hon, I'll go crazy
if you cancel the wedding.

225
00:12:53,272 --> 00:12:54,648
-[Arnaldo] Hey! Hey!
-[Ivy] Please.

226
00:12:54,732 --> 00:12:56,066
Hon.

227
00:12:56,984 --> 00:12:59,403
-It's fine.
-What do you mean?

228
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:03,240
We're fine. I…

229
00:13:04,408 --> 00:13:06,785
-[Ivy] Do you accept my…
-It's fine, now I understand.

230
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:09,246
I appreciate everything.

231
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:12,041
-[relieved sigh]
-[grunts reassuringly]

232
00:13:12,917 --> 00:13:14,210
You love me?

233
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:16,587
I love you very much.

234
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:18,964
Arnaldo, are you sure you love me?

235
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:21,342
I love you so much.

236
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:24,136
Ivy Aguas, I love you so much.

237
00:13:26,096 --> 00:13:27,515
-Thanks, hon.
-[Arnaldo] It may be crazy but…

238
00:13:28,933 --> 00:13:32,686
-I'm also crazily in love with you.
-No, trust me, I'm crazier.

239
00:13:33,771 --> 00:13:35,147
I'm going crazy, Arnaldo.

240
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:37,107
I love you so much. Thank you.

241
00:13:37,858 --> 00:13:38,859
Thanks, hon.

242
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:57,086
[Arnaldo] <i>Who will you meet with, Ivy?</i>

243
00:14:02,424 --> 00:14:03,467
<i>Hon.</i>

244
00:14:08,973 --> 00:14:10,015
<i>Be safe.</i>

245
00:14:29,076 --> 00:14:31,912
Just accept the Jaguar's help.

246
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:36,041
I assure you won't regret it.

247
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:40,588
[tense music]

248
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:46,510
[woman] Hello, everyone!
Vote for the mayor!

249
00:14:46,594 --> 00:14:50,097
Mayor Ardiente is expecting you!
You're all invited!

250
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:52,766
Please be there! Everyone is invited!

251
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:54,977
[woman] What's this new gimmick
of the mayor?

252
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:58,731
Maybe a pronouncement of another lie.

253
00:14:59,064 --> 00:15:00,107
Yeah, right.

254
00:15:00,691 --> 00:15:03,569
[woman] <i>Let's vote for Mayor Arnaldo!</i>

255
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:05,154
<i>Let's show our support!</i>

256
00:15:05,654 --> 00:15:07,239
<i>A great leader of this town!</i>

257
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:10,409
-[woman] Support the Ardientes!
-An event hosted by the family!

258
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:12,202
-Don't miss it!
-Come on!

259
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:14,204
Everyone!

260
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:17,875
We have an invitation
from the rival party.

261
00:15:17,958 --> 00:15:21,629
-[Pandoy] What?
-They said we shouldn't miss it.

262
00:15:38,437 --> 00:15:42,775
If you think that your event
will be a success, Ardientes,

263
00:15:43,567 --> 00:15:44,610
well…

264
00:15:44,944 --> 00:15:45,986
[chuckling]

265
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:48,781
…you're all wrong.

266
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:51,909
Very wrong.

267
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,378
[door squeaks]

268
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:08,258
-Grandpa, you wanted to see me?
-Hi.

269
00:16:10,135 --> 00:16:13,389
Arnaldo, tomorrow is your big day.

270
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:16,350
And I'm sure you're going
to make me proud.

271
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:18,560
I will.

272
00:16:19,561 --> 00:16:23,023
I do feel the pressure
but I'll do my best.

273
00:16:24,608 --> 00:16:26,652
Anyway, that's not the only reason

274
00:16:26,735 --> 00:16:28,362
why I summoned you.

275
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:32,992
What I have here in my hand
is an heirloom.

276
00:16:33,075 --> 00:16:35,536
It's very important to me.

277
00:16:36,829 --> 00:16:39,832
This used to belong
to your great-grandmother.

278
00:16:40,666 --> 00:16:41,667
Now,

279
00:16:43,252 --> 00:16:47,423
I want you to present this
to Ivy as an engagement ring.

280
00:16:49,925 --> 00:16:50,968
Wow!

281
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:56,640
[smirks] Thank you.

282
00:16:58,851 --> 00:16:59,977
Don't thank me yet.

283
00:17:00,936 --> 00:17:03,897
You still have an election to win.

284
00:17:09,653 --> 00:17:13,115
[tense music]

285
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:28,589
[dripping]

286
00:17:58,786 --> 00:17:59,870
[Diego] <i>What do you want from me?</i>

287
00:18:01,038 --> 00:18:02,289
<i>Why are you helping me?</i>

288
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:06,418
<i>Jaguar says he will help you</i>
<i>in your candidacy</i>

289
00:18:06,502 --> 00:18:10,631
<i>by providing money,</i>
<i>personnel, and arsenals.</i>

290
00:18:10,714 --> 00:18:15,719
<i>And Diego, he also guarantees</i>
<i>your victory against Arnaldo.</i>

291
00:18:22,976 --> 00:18:24,853
[Ivy] <i>Don't worry, Diego.</i>

292
00:18:24,937 --> 00:18:28,065
<i>Mom and I will do everything</i>
<i>to get you out of prison.</i>

293
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:31,860
<i>I won't let Arnaldo hurt you.</i>

294
00:18:32,986 --> 00:18:34,196
<i>Please stay safe.</i>

295
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:50,230
Wow!

296
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:52,482
My wife looks stunning today.

297
00:19:52,816 --> 00:19:55,652
Your heels and necklace suit you.

298
00:19:56,737 --> 00:19:58,197
That's ruby, isn't it? Your birthstone.

299
00:20:02,743 --> 00:20:05,078
[Emilia] Arnaldo, where's Ivy?

300
00:20:05,621 --> 00:20:08,165
Ivy will meet us at the venue.

301
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:11,293
Grandpa is waiting outside. So, let's go?

302
00:20:11,376 --> 00:20:13,837
-Our supporters are waiting.
-Let's go.

303
00:20:17,591 --> 00:20:20,344
-[crowd chattering]
-[brass music playing]

304
00:20:20,427 --> 00:20:21,929
[Arnaldo] I expect your support
in the election.

305
00:20:22,304 --> 00:20:23,597
Thank you so much.

306
00:20:24,223 --> 00:20:25,265
That's what I like.

307
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:27,976
I always see you around.

308
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:32,105
Thank you so much for gracing my events.

309
00:20:36,485 --> 00:20:39,863
[Arnaldo laughing] That's great.
Really great.

310
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:42,407
-We'll further boost it.
-[man] Yeah.

311
00:20:42,783 --> 00:20:43,951
[Arnaldo] Yeah, good.

312
00:20:45,327 --> 00:20:48,789
The other party has no match against me.

313
00:20:49,081 --> 00:20:52,209
I am rightful to serve, not those…

314
00:20:56,588 --> 00:21:00,217
[men] <i>Julio! Julio! Julio! Julio!</i>

315
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:04,888
<i>Julio! Julio! Julio! Julio!</i>

316
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:06,556
<i>Julio! Julio!</i>

317
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:15,357
Terrific! Thanks.

318
00:21:16,984 --> 00:21:18,193
Hon!

319
00:21:18,735 --> 00:21:19,778
Hon!

320
00:21:21,905 --> 00:21:23,657
-You look beautiful.
-[Ivy] Thank you.

321
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:24,783
Are you ready?

322
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:28,412
I'll publicly introduce you
as the future first lady

323
00:21:28,495 --> 00:21:29,955
of Poblacion Ardiente.

324
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:42,259
-[brass music playing]
-[people cheering]

325
00:22:03,405 --> 00:22:06,283
Everyone, let us all welcome

326
00:22:06,908 --> 00:22:11,747
-Congressman Julio Ardiente!
-[crowd applauding]

327
00:22:11,830 --> 00:22:14,833
[emcee] Former Governor
Emilia Ardiente-Torillo

328
00:22:14,916 --> 00:22:17,544
and her husband, Mister Raul Torillo.

329
00:22:19,296 --> 00:22:23,550
-Miss Clarita de Guzman.
-[crowd applauding]

330
00:22:23,633 --> 00:22:26,553
-Miss Ivy Aguas.
-[crowd applauding]

331
00:22:29,056 --> 00:22:31,975
And of course, our beloved mayor

332
00:22:32,059 --> 00:22:35,479
and the future governor
of Poblacion Ardiente,

333
00:22:35,562 --> 00:22:38,356
Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo!

334
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:43,653
-[crowd cheering loudly]
-[brass music playing]

335
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:53,914
[Arnaldo] Everyone,
please take your seats.

336
00:22:53,997 --> 00:22:56,541
-[chuckles]
-[woman] I love you, Mayor!

337
00:22:56,625 --> 00:22:59,544
-I love you too!
-[crowd cheering]

338
00:23:02,005 --> 00:23:05,342
[Arnaldo] Good morning,
Poblacion Ardiente!

339
00:23:05,425 --> 00:23:08,303
[crowd applauding]

340
00:23:08,386 --> 00:23:11,640
I am extremely glad that you've joined us

341
00:23:11,723 --> 00:23:13,892
for this very important event.

342
00:23:15,102 --> 00:23:16,436
I love you all

343
00:23:16,520 --> 00:23:18,897
that's why I want you all to be part

344
00:23:19,523 --> 00:23:23,068
of my life as your future governor.

345
00:23:23,151 --> 00:23:25,278
[crowd applauding]

346
00:23:26,571 --> 00:23:30,200
Today, let me introduce to all of you

347
00:23:30,283 --> 00:23:33,203
your future first lady.

348
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:37,874
She is the woman who captured my heart.

349
00:23:38,542 --> 00:23:43,505
The woman who continuously
makes the Ardientes stronger!

350
00:23:46,341 --> 00:23:47,384
Everyone,

351
00:23:48,969 --> 00:23:52,889
my most beloved lady, Ivy Aguas!

352
00:23:52,973 --> 00:23:57,519
[crowd cheering loudly]

353
00:23:57,602 --> 00:24:00,689
[tense music playing]

354
00:24:03,775 --> 00:24:04,734
Please.

355
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:11,533
Hon, I know I already proposed to you,

356
00:24:11,616 --> 00:24:13,410
but it would be even better

357
00:24:13,493 --> 00:24:16,830
if the people of Ardiente
witnessed this moment

358
00:24:17,414 --> 00:24:19,624
[applause, crowd cheering]

359
00:24:19,708 --> 00:24:21,209
If it's okay with you,

360
00:24:21,293 --> 00:24:23,253
I'd like to ask for your hand once again

361
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:26,798
in front of our supporters.

362
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:31,469
[crowd cheering]

363
00:24:33,847 --> 00:24:35,765
Ivy Aguas,

364
00:24:35,849 --> 00:24:37,934
[crowd clapping]

365
00:24:38,018 --> 00:24:39,269
I love you so much.

366
00:24:39,352 --> 00:24:40,437
[crowd cheering]

367
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:42,189
Will you marry me?

368
00:24:42,272 --> 00:24:46,151
-[crowd cheering louder]
-[Arnaldo laughs]

369
00:24:48,612 --> 00:24:50,697
-Yes! Yes!
-Yes!

370
00:24:55,702 --> 00:24:57,996
[crowd cheering]

371
00:24:58,997 --> 00:25:00,707
[woman] Viva Ardiente!

372
00:25:00,790 --> 00:25:01,917
[shutter clicks]

373
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:04,252
[crowd cheering]

374
00:25:04,336 --> 00:25:06,129
[Arnaldo] Flowers for you, of course.

375
00:25:08,506 --> 00:25:09,549
[shutter clicks]

376
00:25:11,509 --> 00:25:12,552
Viva Ardiente!

377
00:25:12,636 --> 00:25:14,179
[crowd] Viva Ardiente!

378
00:25:14,262 --> 00:25:17,015
[brass music playing]

379
00:25:18,516 --> 00:25:20,560
-Congratulations, Governor.
-Thank you. Thank you.

380
00:25:20,644 --> 00:25:22,896
[brass music playing]

381
00:25:30,487 --> 00:25:31,613
Viva Ardiente!

382
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:33,865
Viva Ardiente!

383
00:25:37,077 --> 00:25:40,455
[Arnaldo] Okay, I have more
good news for you.

384
00:25:40,956 --> 00:25:46,628
Now, I'll share with you
my provincial platforms!

385
00:25:51,633 --> 00:25:53,051
[woman] You're only going
to manipulate us,

386
00:25:53,134 --> 00:25:55,595
just like what you did to that woman!

387
00:25:56,429 --> 00:26:00,684
[crowd booing]

388
00:26:03,561 --> 00:26:04,604
[Arnaldo] Ahh…

389
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:07,107
These projects we'll be?

390
00:26:07,190 --> 00:26:08,942
[Diego] Instead of public service,

391
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:11,987
you'll only make them suffer!

392
00:26:19,369 --> 00:26:24,416
[crowd] <i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

393
00:26:24,791 --> 00:26:28,586
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

394
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:32,048
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

395
00:26:32,382 --> 00:26:35,719
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

396
00:26:36,177 --> 00:26:39,472
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

397
00:26:40,181 --> 00:26:43,601
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

398
00:26:44,060 --> 00:26:47,314
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

399
00:26:47,939 --> 00:26:51,109
What now?! Were you surprised?!

400
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:54,946
Yes, I'm a free man now!

401
00:26:55,655 --> 00:26:59,242
And you can never imprison me again!

402
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:01,619
It's your family
that needs to be imprisoned!

403
00:27:01,953 --> 00:27:03,246
You will go down!

404
00:27:03,830 --> 00:27:07,334
And a new Ardiente will be reborn

405
00:27:07,709 --> 00:27:10,545
that is governed by the people!

406
00:27:10,962 --> 00:27:13,173
For a new Ardiente!

407
00:27:13,548 --> 00:27:17,052
[crowd] <i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

408
00:27:17,135 --> 00:27:20,513
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

409
00:27:20,597 --> 00:27:23,892
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

410
00:27:34,778 --> 00:27:35,820
Diego.

411
00:27:37,697 --> 00:27:40,325
This event and the public governance

412
00:27:40,408 --> 00:27:42,494
are only for the worthy,

413
00:27:43,745 --> 00:27:46,956
not for ex-convicts like you.

414
00:27:48,500 --> 00:27:49,959
Lies!

415
00:27:52,545 --> 00:27:54,714
The Court is the one who absolved me.

416
00:27:55,382 --> 00:27:59,177
I was never sentenced,
so I'm not an ex-convict!

417
00:28:00,011 --> 00:28:01,346
What about you, Arnaldo?!

418
00:28:02,389 --> 00:28:04,182
When will you go to prison

419
00:28:04,265 --> 00:28:06,351
for all the crimes that you committed?!

420
00:28:06,893 --> 00:28:09,354
[crowd murmuring]

421
00:28:09,604 --> 00:28:13,608
-Diego! Diego!
-Boo!

422
00:28:19,489 --> 00:28:22,534
[crowd] <i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

423
00:28:23,743 --> 00:28:25,120
Diego has been freed?

424
00:28:25,412 --> 00:28:29,374
Doesn't that mean he agreed
to the terms of Jaguar?!

425
00:28:30,250 --> 00:28:33,378
Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

426
00:28:34,003 --> 00:28:36,506
What's important
is that Diego is free now.

427
00:28:36,923 --> 00:28:41,219
The rightful future governor
has been freed.

428
00:28:41,302 --> 00:28:42,512
Miss Camia is right.

429
00:28:42,595 --> 00:28:43,722
[Arnaldo] Crimes?

430
00:28:44,389 --> 00:28:46,057
What crimes are you talking about?

431
00:28:46,725 --> 00:28:48,518
[crowd] Yeah, right!

432
00:28:49,102 --> 00:28:52,021
You tried to kill me inside the jail,

433
00:28:52,522 --> 00:28:55,859
and worst is you killed Nimfa Naig!

434
00:28:55,942 --> 00:28:57,610
-That's true!
-[crowd] Yeah, right!

435
00:28:57,694 --> 00:28:58,945
Boo!

436
00:28:59,028 --> 00:29:02,657
[crowd clamoring]

437
00:29:09,622 --> 00:29:14,169
There's no evidence
to support your accusations!

438
00:29:14,252 --> 00:29:15,670
We are not stupid!

439
00:29:17,380 --> 00:29:19,007
We all know

440
00:29:19,549 --> 00:29:23,803
that the Ardientes hold
the law in this land!

441
00:29:23,887 --> 00:29:26,598
-[Arnaldo chuckles]
-[crowd clamoring]

442
00:29:27,682 --> 00:29:30,435
Says the man who's supposed
to be in prison but is now free!

443
00:29:30,977 --> 00:29:33,438
Maybe you're the one who's abusing power?

444
00:29:33,521 --> 00:29:36,524
-[crowd] Yeah, right!
-[Arnaldo] Now what?

445
00:29:38,276 --> 00:29:41,988
Diego, my little brother,
stop spreading lies.

446
00:29:42,071 --> 00:29:44,532
I didn't know you came here
just to crack jokes.

447
00:29:45,617 --> 00:29:46,659
[chuckles]

448
00:29:47,827 --> 00:29:49,662
Laugh while you can, Arnaldo.

449
00:29:50,580 --> 00:29:53,875
Because once I kick you out
of the capitol,

450
00:29:53,958 --> 00:29:57,420
I'll make sure to deal with you first!

451
00:29:58,129 --> 00:30:01,257
I'll serve justice and punishment

452
00:30:01,341 --> 00:30:03,676
for all your crimes!

453
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:06,721
[crowd clamoring]

454
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:07,722
Yeah, that's right!

455
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:10,350
The Ardientes should pay
for all their crimes!

456
00:30:10,892 --> 00:30:12,602
Diego for Governor!

457
00:30:12,685 --> 00:30:15,688
[crowd] <i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

458
00:30:15,772 --> 00:30:18,983
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

459
00:30:19,567 --> 00:30:22,695
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

460
00:30:22,779 --> 00:30:26,032
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

461
00:30:26,407 --> 00:30:29,702
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

462
00:30:30,745 --> 00:30:32,038
<i>Diego! Diego!</i>

463
00:30:33,122 --> 00:30:34,249
[screams]

464
00:30:35,500 --> 00:30:36,709
Arrest that criminal!

465
00:30:37,210 --> 00:30:40,129
[Camia] You have no right to arrest Diego!

466
00:30:40,505 --> 00:30:43,800
He's innocent! Fight him fair and square!

467
00:30:43,883 --> 00:30:45,009
Shut up!

468
00:30:45,093 --> 00:30:48,137
You damn trespassers! Get the hell out!

469
00:30:48,763 --> 00:30:52,725
We're residents of this town!
We were invited!

470
00:30:53,601 --> 00:30:55,687
[crowd] That's right!

471
00:30:56,104 --> 00:30:58,022
Diego! Diego!

472
00:30:59,899 --> 00:31:02,610
I don't care! Shut up!

473
00:31:03,194 --> 00:31:04,571
-[crowd] <i>Diego! Diego!</i>
-[Arnaldo] Get out!

474
00:31:05,154 --> 00:31:07,407
-Hon!
-[crowd] <i>Diego! Diego!</i>

475
00:31:07,490 --> 00:31:09,033
[Ivy] Hon! No! Let go!

476
00:31:09,909 --> 00:31:10,952
Hon!

477
00:31:13,204 --> 00:31:14,789
Shut up!

478
00:31:16,207 --> 00:31:17,375
Silence, all of you!

479
00:31:18,001 --> 00:31:19,502
What are you so smug about?

480
00:31:20,503 --> 00:31:25,341
Is this the future of Poblacion Ardiente?!

481
00:31:26,885 --> 00:31:30,471
A town full of unruly citizens?!

482
00:31:31,389 --> 00:31:33,057
You uncivilized people!

483
00:31:34,601 --> 00:31:36,394
You said you were invited!

484
00:31:36,769 --> 00:31:38,897
What for?! To cause ruckus?!

485
00:31:40,398 --> 00:31:44,193
Is this the kind of future
you want for your kids?!

486
00:31:45,778 --> 00:31:47,530
Are you really the future leaders

487
00:31:48,323 --> 00:31:49,657
of this province?!

488
00:31:50,533 --> 00:31:55,371
You will do anything
for the throne and power!

489
00:31:56,080 --> 00:32:00,209
You better look in the mirror
before you criticize!

490
00:32:00,293 --> 00:32:02,337
You damn hypocrites!

491
00:32:03,421 --> 00:32:04,339
[derisive scoff]

492
00:32:05,006 --> 00:32:07,342
Arnaldo! Let's go!

493
00:32:09,969 --> 00:32:13,348
[crowd] <i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

494
00:32:13,431 --> 00:32:16,559
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

495
00:32:16,935 --> 00:32:20,897
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

496
00:32:20,980 --> 00:32:24,233
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

497
00:32:24,317 --> 00:32:26,736
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

498
00:32:27,862 --> 00:32:31,616
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

499
00:32:33,242 --> 00:32:34,285
No!

500
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:38,206
[crowd] <i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

501
00:32:38,790 --> 00:32:41,918
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

502
00:32:42,251 --> 00:32:45,380
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

503
00:32:45,755 --> 00:32:48,925
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

504
00:32:49,425 --> 00:32:52,637
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

505
00:32:53,054 --> 00:32:57,433
<i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

506
00:32:57,517 --> 00:33:00,561
Lara, issue a press release

507
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:04,732
denying everything that happened
in that stupid charade!

508
00:33:05,358 --> 00:33:08,236
But, Congressman, the news is everywhere.

509
00:33:08,945 --> 00:33:11,030
The only way to turn this around

510
00:33:11,114 --> 00:33:13,282
is to apologize
to the camp of Diego Torillo

511
00:33:13,366 --> 00:33:14,742
for poking that gun.

512
00:33:15,410 --> 00:33:16,953
Apologize?!

513
00:33:17,370 --> 00:33:18,788
[smirks] Yeah, right!

514
00:33:19,205 --> 00:33:20,581
And the moon that's hanging up there

515
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:21,958
is made out of cheese!

516
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:25,461
What's wrong with you?!
There's no gun pointing!

517
00:33:25,545 --> 00:33:27,422
Arnaldo did not point his gun!

518
00:33:27,505 --> 00:33:31,134
He didn't do anything wrong!
It's their word against ours!

519
00:33:31,718 --> 00:33:34,137
And their words don't matter anyway.

520
00:33:34,220 --> 00:33:35,179
[chuckles]

521
00:33:35,263 --> 00:33:37,932
Here comes Lady Godiva on her high horse.

522
00:33:38,016 --> 00:33:39,183
[Lara] Excuse me, sir.

523
00:33:40,018 --> 00:33:41,936
Well, Emilia, where is your son?!

524
00:33:42,729 --> 00:33:45,106
Well, your favorite grandson
is still sleeping.

525
00:33:48,484 --> 00:33:52,572
The reputation of Arnaldo
is already ruined, Papa.

526
00:33:52,655 --> 00:33:55,491
Why won't you let me run
for governor, instead?

527
00:33:55,575 --> 00:33:59,037
Emilia, please! Stay out of this.

528
00:33:59,746 --> 00:34:02,957
Because no matter what happens,
Arnaldo, your son,

529
00:34:03,958 --> 00:34:07,128
is a hundred times
better a choice for governor

530
00:34:07,211 --> 00:34:08,463
than you will ever be.

531
00:34:08,796 --> 00:34:12,592
So, please, just do what you have to do!

532
00:34:14,218 --> 00:34:16,429
Okay, Papa. I will wake him up.

533
00:34:23,436 --> 00:34:26,731
Diego shouldn't have gotten out of prison.

534
00:34:30,443 --> 00:34:33,071
The evidence is rock solid.

535
00:34:34,781 --> 00:34:37,825
It's perfectly planned.
He shouldn't have gotten out.

536
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:39,827
Oh, Honey, let's go.

537
00:34:41,579 --> 00:34:43,289
We're going to be late for our meeting.

538
00:34:43,372 --> 00:34:44,290
Are you happy?

539
00:34:46,209 --> 00:34:47,251
Happy?

540
00:34:48,461 --> 00:34:52,590
Are you happy that Diego is now free?

541
00:34:55,384 --> 00:34:56,427
[smirks]

542
00:34:57,053 --> 00:34:58,096
See.

543
00:34:59,472 --> 00:35:01,432
That's what I've been asking myself.

544
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,602
Why are you always ambiguous

545
00:35:04,685 --> 00:35:06,896
when it comes to my lovely brother?

546
00:35:07,522 --> 00:35:09,190
Why can't you just pick a side?

547
00:35:10,691 --> 00:35:11,859
My side!

548
00:35:13,444 --> 00:35:14,445
Is that difficult?

549
00:35:17,615 --> 00:35:18,699
Honey.

550
00:35:23,955 --> 00:35:28,584
You know that I believe in you.

551
00:35:30,837 --> 00:35:34,632
[Ivy] <i>I believe that you will fall soon.</i>

552
00:35:36,175 --> 00:35:40,054
I did everything to win.

553
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:45,643
[mumbling] I did everything…

554
00:35:46,769 --> 00:35:51,107
[Ivy] <i>Just a little more evidence</i>
<i>will secure your loss.</i>

555
00:35:55,945 --> 00:35:57,572
DIEGO FOR THE NEW ARDIENTE

556
00:35:57,655 --> 00:35:58,948
You were right.

557
00:36:00,449 --> 00:36:02,910
I accepted the support of Jaguar.

558
00:36:02,994 --> 00:36:05,872
[somber music playing]

559
00:36:05,955 --> 00:36:09,792
Diego, you know what Jaguar
wants in return.

560
00:36:11,002 --> 00:36:12,712
He's going to control you.

561
00:36:12,795 --> 00:36:15,423
But he doesn't want anything in return.

562
00:36:16,507 --> 00:36:18,301
What do you mean?

563
00:36:28,436 --> 00:36:29,478
[cop] <i>Diego!</i>

564
00:36:34,066 --> 00:36:36,861
-<i>Yes?</i>
-[cop] <i>Just follow me.</i>

565
00:36:41,949 --> 00:36:43,784
Your attorney didn't tell us about this.

566
00:36:44,327 --> 00:36:45,745
Does she know about this?

567
00:36:46,537 --> 00:36:47,580
Not yet.

568
00:36:48,372 --> 00:36:50,249
Everything happened so fast.

569
00:36:51,834 --> 00:36:53,044
Honestly, Diego.

570
00:36:54,003 --> 00:36:57,715
Do you really think Jaguar
got you out of prison?

571
00:36:58,966 --> 00:37:00,051
I'm not sure, Auntie.

572
00:37:01,302 --> 00:37:04,305
But if he did, I didn't ask for it,

573
00:37:04,388 --> 00:37:06,307
and I didn't agree to his terms.

574
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:11,479
But I won't deny myself this freedom.

575
00:37:11,562 --> 00:37:15,191
[Loring] But what if he returns
and demands payment?

576
00:37:16,317 --> 00:37:17,360
Well, whatever happens,

577
00:37:17,944 --> 00:37:19,111
I'll stay out of trouble.

578
00:37:19,904 --> 00:37:20,988
[Camia] Yes, you should.

579
00:37:21,781 --> 00:37:24,533
And if that Jaguar really is behind this,

580
00:37:24,617 --> 00:37:27,453
I hope this is the last time
he is involved with you.

581
00:37:38,047 --> 00:37:39,090
It's good!

582
00:37:40,508 --> 00:37:44,387
Anyway, we knew that case wouldn't stick.

583
00:37:45,304 --> 00:37:46,389
But…

584
00:37:48,057 --> 00:37:51,310
Diego was released earlier than expected.

585
00:37:55,147 --> 00:37:57,858
Hon, if I remember correctly,
you had Diego imprisoned.

586
00:38:01,654 --> 00:38:02,697
Miss Aguas!

587
00:38:03,239 --> 00:38:04,573
You seem shocked!

588
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:09,370
Welcome to the world of politics.

589
00:38:09,453 --> 00:38:10,997
You're not new to this.

590
00:38:13,916 --> 00:38:18,421
We stop at nothing
to make sure that we win.

591
00:38:19,213 --> 00:38:20,631
[in French] <i>That's life, that's war.</i>

592
00:38:21,257 --> 00:38:26,971
Now the rest, we attribute
to collateral damage.

593
00:38:28,139 --> 00:38:31,517
Ivy, why so concerned?

594
00:38:32,143 --> 00:38:33,352
And may I ask you?

595
00:38:33,436 --> 00:38:36,355
Who are you worried about,
Arnaldo or Diego?

596
00:38:37,231 --> 00:38:39,692
[Ivy] Future mother-in-law,
you shouldn't be asking that.

597
00:38:40,234 --> 00:38:42,278
Because I'm going to marry Arnaldo.

598
00:38:43,237 --> 00:38:44,447
You should know the answer.

599
00:38:44,822 --> 00:38:46,324
Just making sure.

600
00:38:47,366 --> 00:38:48,659
[clapping] Good!

601
00:38:49,285 --> 00:38:51,203
Now, where was I?

602
00:38:52,496 --> 00:38:54,415
Oh! Diego!

603
00:38:55,458 --> 00:38:59,045
You know, we have to show
the other side of Diego

604
00:38:59,128 --> 00:39:01,881
to the voters of this town.

605
00:39:02,548 --> 00:39:07,094
That Diego is not as clean
as he presents himself to be.

606
00:39:07,928 --> 00:39:09,805
We should gather…

607
00:39:10,264 --> 00:39:11,390
Emilia, that's your job.

608
00:39:12,558 --> 00:39:15,561
…that Diego also receives help

609
00:39:15,644 --> 00:39:19,940
from criminals like Jaguar,

610
00:39:20,483 --> 00:39:23,361
which will make him a hypocrite and…

611
00:39:25,488 --> 00:39:27,990
-a liar just like us.
-[laughing]

612
00:39:29,158 --> 00:39:30,201
Yes, Papa.

613
00:39:30,993 --> 00:39:33,329
If Jaguar really helped Diego,

614
00:39:33,412 --> 00:39:34,955
I'm sure the two will definitely meet.

615
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:36,582
I'll take care of it, Papa.

616
00:39:37,958 --> 00:39:39,168
Okay.

617
00:39:39,251 --> 00:39:40,586
[Emilia] Arnaldo, are you okay?

618
00:39:41,295 --> 00:39:44,965
You seem bothered again!
You're always like that!

619
00:39:57,770 --> 00:40:00,356
Batch, this is our schedule
for the next two weeks.

620
00:40:00,773 --> 00:40:02,525
It's crunch time as the election nears,

621
00:40:02,608 --> 00:40:04,902
so we have to accomplish everything here.

622
00:40:05,444 --> 00:40:06,612
Check this for approval.

623
00:40:07,446 --> 00:40:09,323
-This is good, batch.
-Okay.

624
00:40:09,407 --> 00:40:12,785
Have you finished the costing
of the materials we need?

625
00:40:16,163 --> 00:40:17,957
-Batch, excuse me.
-[Marlon] Sure.

626
00:40:22,962 --> 00:40:25,840
-Hello, Ivy.
-Diego, how are you?

627
00:40:26,298 --> 00:40:27,758
Are you sure no one is hearing you?

628
00:40:27,842 --> 00:40:29,969
Yeah, I'm safe. I'm at home right now.

629
00:40:30,928 --> 00:40:32,680
Diego, I'm worried about you.

630
00:40:32,763 --> 00:40:34,723
Ivy, I'm fine and free.

631
00:40:35,474 --> 00:40:36,517
Can I meet with you?

632
00:40:36,976 --> 00:40:38,227
With what happened earlier,

633
00:40:38,310 --> 00:40:41,230
the Ardientes will keep their eyes on you.

634
00:40:41,897 --> 00:40:44,859
By the way, I'm looking for more evidence

635
00:40:44,942 --> 00:40:46,694
against the Ardientes.

636
00:40:46,944 --> 00:40:48,154
Be careful.

637
00:40:48,237 --> 00:40:50,239
It's you who should be more careful.

638
00:40:50,322 --> 00:40:53,534
The Ardientes might use
your connections with Jaguar…

639
00:40:54,034 --> 00:40:56,787
-<i>to ruin you.</i>
-They can't do that to me.

640
00:40:57,204 --> 00:40:58,414
Just be careful.

641
00:41:03,002 --> 00:41:05,129
[Julio on audio record]
<i>Miss Aguas! You seem shocked!</i>

642
00:41:05,212 --> 00:41:06,881
<i>You're not new to this.</i>

643
00:41:07,214 --> 00:41:11,802
<i>We stop at nothing</i>
<i>to make sure that we win.</i>

644
00:41:13,554 --> 00:41:14,889
[Emilia] <i>Who are you worried about,</i>

645
00:41:14,972 --> 00:41:17,766
<i>Arnaldo or Diego?</i>

646
00:41:18,809 --> 00:41:20,561
[Ivy] <i>I'm going to marry Arnaldo.</i>

647
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:23,481
-<i>You should know the answer.</i>
-[Emilia] <i>Just making sure.</i>

648
00:41:29,528 --> 00:41:30,613
[Ivy] <i>This is not enough.</i>

649
00:41:31,822 --> 00:41:35,826
<i>I have to make Arnaldo confess</i>
<i>to the crimes he committed.</i>

650
00:41:42,208 --> 00:41:43,250
[Raul] Emilia.

651
00:41:45,377 --> 00:41:47,755
You look stressed again.
What's the matter?

652
00:41:48,631 --> 00:41:52,426
I am stressed about Papa's task.

653
00:41:53,135 --> 00:41:56,805
Task? What task? Maybe I can help you?

654
00:41:58,224 --> 00:42:00,726
I need to deliver your replacement's head.

655
00:42:01,519 --> 00:42:02,895
[clicks tongue] So, it's Jaguar again.

656
00:42:02,978 --> 00:42:06,148
[chuckling] I'm just laughing
when you mention him.

657
00:42:06,232 --> 00:42:07,483
First of all,

658
00:42:08,442 --> 00:42:11,779
since when did you lower your standards?

659
00:42:12,404 --> 00:42:15,908
You haven't even seen that man's face.

660
00:42:16,575 --> 00:42:17,910
Suddenly, he's your type?

661
00:42:18,744 --> 00:42:21,872
Emilia, that man is always wearing a mask

662
00:42:21,956 --> 00:42:26,043
because he thinks he'll need it
for the rest of his life.

663
00:42:26,126 --> 00:42:27,962
I bet he looks like a bug.

664
00:42:29,296 --> 00:42:30,297
-Hmm.
-Right?

665
00:42:30,381 --> 00:42:31,882
[laughing]

666
00:42:31,966 --> 00:42:34,718
Raul, look. He gave me this.

667
00:42:37,846 --> 00:42:40,182
Well, I remember on our wedding day,

668
00:42:40,266 --> 00:42:41,892
you also gave me one of these.

669
00:42:41,976 --> 00:42:44,103
You said you bought it with your savings.

670
00:42:44,186 --> 00:42:47,231
But it turns out,
you just asked Papa for it.

671
00:42:47,856 --> 00:42:50,025
But it's fine. It's still sweet, though.

672
00:42:54,738 --> 00:42:58,659
So, you think this Jaguar guy
is copying me, huh?

673
00:42:59,827 --> 00:43:02,830
Maybe he's imitating me
but he can't really pull it off.

674
00:43:02,913 --> 00:43:05,291
First of all, his style
is different from mine,

675
00:43:05,958 --> 00:43:07,209
like giving gifts.

676
00:43:07,293 --> 00:43:08,794
You said it yourself,

677
00:43:08,877 --> 00:43:11,589
I need to ask for money to buy you gifts.

678
00:43:12,214 --> 00:43:15,843
I'm straightforward about what I want.

679
00:43:16,427 --> 00:43:18,679
Like how I got you.

680
00:43:19,138 --> 00:43:22,099
I don't beat around the bush
or charm you with gifts.

681
00:43:22,516 --> 00:43:24,059
I tell people if I like them.

682
00:43:25,019 --> 00:43:26,103
So tell me,

683
00:43:27,146 --> 00:43:28,272
do you love me?

684
00:43:30,816 --> 00:43:31,900
Yes.

685
00:43:32,234 --> 00:43:33,819
I can't feel it, Emilia.

686
00:43:35,321 --> 00:43:37,114
-I love you.
-Really?

687
00:43:38,115 --> 00:43:39,074
Then kiss me.

688
00:43:40,492 --> 00:43:41,493
[chuckling]

689
00:43:44,663 --> 00:43:46,373
-[both chuckling]
-That's it?

690
00:44:15,027 --> 00:44:17,071
[phone ringing]

691
00:44:17,154 --> 00:44:18,947
-Emilia.
-Hmm?

692
00:44:19,031 --> 00:44:23,452
[ringing continues]

693
00:44:24,453 --> 00:44:26,538
Looks like I set the alarm wrong again.

694
00:44:29,375 --> 00:44:30,542
Where are you going?

695
00:44:30,626 --> 00:44:33,212
-To the salon.
-All right.

696
00:44:34,838 --> 00:44:39,551
[tense music]

697
00:44:48,811 --> 00:44:49,895
[Rufo] Ma'am.

698
00:44:55,859 --> 00:44:56,902
[sighs]

699
00:45:03,742 --> 00:45:05,202
Come on, Jaguar.

700
00:45:05,285 --> 00:45:08,122
Didn't I tell you
not to make surprise visits?

701
00:45:08,747 --> 00:45:09,957
But, you called, right?

702
00:45:12,584 --> 00:45:13,627
Yes.

703
00:45:15,504 --> 00:45:17,381
I called because I wanted to know

704
00:45:17,464 --> 00:45:20,134
if you're behind the release of Diego.

705
00:45:20,426 --> 00:45:22,803
Emilia, if that's the only reason

706
00:45:22,886 --> 00:45:24,096
why you asked me to come,

707
00:45:24,179 --> 00:45:26,140
then I'm just wasting my time.

708
00:45:26,557 --> 00:45:28,600
Can you please just answer the question?!

709
00:45:28,809 --> 00:45:29,852
I'll only answer

710
00:45:29,935 --> 00:45:32,312
once you've decided to cooperate with me.

711
00:45:36,859 --> 00:45:37,901
[Rufo] Ma'am.

712
00:46:05,137 --> 00:46:06,472
What are you doing here?!

713
00:46:16,356 --> 00:46:18,025
Why are you here?

714
00:46:18,108 --> 00:46:20,444
Didn't your message say that
you'd leave me alone?

715
00:46:21,570 --> 00:46:23,947
You're right.
I'm just assuring your safety.

716
00:46:25,365 --> 00:46:26,617
Why are you doing this?

717
00:46:27,910 --> 00:46:29,953
What do you want
in exchange for all this?!

718
00:46:30,662 --> 00:46:33,957
The same thing you want,
the demise of the Ardientes.

719
00:46:35,584 --> 00:46:37,628
I'm sure that's what you want, right?

720
00:46:39,505 --> 00:46:43,550
[tense music]

721
00:46:58,524 --> 00:47:02,194
[Emilia] <i>Finally,</i>
<i>this will bring you down,</i>

722
00:47:02,277 --> 00:47:03,820
<i>Diego Torillo.</i>

723
00:47:09,701 --> 00:47:11,286
[Camia] <i>What will you do now, Lily?</i>

724
00:47:11,370 --> 00:47:13,664
<i>How are we going to fight Arnaldo?</i>

725
00:47:13,747 --> 00:47:14,790
<i>By force.</i>

726
00:47:16,500 --> 00:47:17,709
[Ivy] <i>I'll drive him insane.</i>

727
00:47:17,793 --> 00:47:19,586
<i>I will grind and break him apart.</i>

728
00:47:19,670 --> 00:47:20,671
-[Arnaldo] <i>Leave!</i>
-[Ivy] <i>Stop!</i>

729
00:47:20,754 --> 00:47:23,715
[Ivy] <i>Emilia and Julio will also go crazy</i>

730
00:47:23,799 --> 00:47:25,884
<i>because of what's happening to Arnaldo.</i>

731
00:47:25,968 --> 00:47:27,553
<i>Ever since you became his fiancé,</i>

732
00:47:27,636 --> 00:47:29,054
<i>-he's started acting crazy!</i>
<i>-That's enough!</i>

733
00:47:29,137 --> 00:47:30,347
[Emilia] <i>You won't attend the debate!</i>

734
00:47:30,430 --> 00:47:32,224
<i>You'll only look like a fool, Arnaldo!</i>

735
00:47:32,307 --> 00:47:35,185
[supporters] <i>Diego Torillo for governor!</i>

736
00:47:35,269 --> 00:47:36,895
[supporters] <i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

737
00:47:38,272 --> 00:47:39,439
[Arnaldo] <i>Who did this?!</i>

738
00:47:39,523 --> 00:47:42,359
[crowd clamoring]

739
00:47:42,985 --> 00:47:45,654
[theme music playing]
